<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct industrial output up revised 3.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct industrial output up revised 3.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in October increased a revised 3.9 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 3.5 percent increase, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month on month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  OCT     PRELIM   MONTH AGO  OCT INDEX</p>
<p> Output		 +3.9    +3.5   +1.5	101.5</p>
<p> Shipments	    +3.7    +3.3   +1.8	103.0</p>
<p> Inventories	  +0.7    +0.6   -1.0	108.4</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p> Shipments ratio    -4.0    -3.7   -0.9	111.2</p>
<p>Unadjusted year on year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   OCT	PRELIM     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +6.5     +6.0	+3.8</p>
<p> Shipments		     +6.8     +6.4	+3.6</p>
<p> Inventories		   -0.1     -0.2	+0.3</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p> Shipments ratio	     -5.7     -5.5	-1.2</p>
</text>
